### **Sexual Assault and Misconduct Reporting Requirements in South Australia**

- **Incident Reporting**: Any suspected or alleged incidents of sexual assault or misconduct within a SA Health facility must be reported and managed according to specific policies [1](https://www.voc.sa.gov.au/the-crime/types-of-crime/sexual-assaults).
- **Criminal Law Consolidation Act 1935 (SA)**: This Act outlines major sexual offences, including rape, unlawful sexual intercourse, and indecent assault [2](https://lawhandbook.sa.gov.au/ch12s09.php).
- **Victims of Crime South Australia**: Defines sexual assault broadly, covering unwanted sexual behaviours such as unwanted touching, kissing, sexual harassment, coerced sexual activity, and rape [1](https://www.voc.sa.gov.au/the-crime/types-of-crime/sexual-assaults).
- **Review of Sexual Consent Laws**: The Attorney-General's Department is reviewing South Australia's sexual consent laws, considering reforms such as an affirmative consent model and increased penalties for image-based sexual offences [3](https://www.agd.sa.gov.au/law-and-justice/consultation/review-of-sexual-consent-laws-in-south-australia).

These requirements ensure that incidents of sexual assault and misconduct are reported and managed appropriately, promoting safety and accountability within healthcare facilities.

[1](https://www.voc.sa.gov.au/the-crime/types-of-crime/sexual-assaults): [Victims of Crime South Australia](https://www.voc.sa.gov.au/the-crime/types-of-crime/sexual-assaults)
[3](https://www.agd.sa.gov.au/law-and-justice/consultation/review-of-sexual-consent-laws-in-south-australia): [Attorney-General's Department](https://www.agd.sa.gov.au/law-and-justice/consultation/review-of-sexual-consent-laws-in-south-australia)
[2](https://lawhandbook.sa.gov.au/ch12s09.php): [Criminal Law Consolidation Act 1935 (SA)](https://lawhandbook.sa.gov.au/ch12s09.php)